<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ha'il</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Hayil</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ha'il is a city in north-central Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>, capital of Ha'il Province, between the Aja and Salma mountains. It was the capital of the Rashidi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of Jabal Shammar from 1836, a stop on pilgrim and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caravan-trade">caravan routes</a>, and in the late 19th century the seat of the most powerful state in central Arabia. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-saud">Ibn Saud</a> captured it in 1921. Rock art sites in the region are on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco">UNESCO</a> World Heritage list.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hail.jpg" alt="Ha'il" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Khalid Alhallabi · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D8%AD%D8%A7%D8%A6%D9%84_-_panoramio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
